{"t":1792415501,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"d48e42c9-a551-4b00-8d7d-28e97a8c676d","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-19T07:47:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 190747\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n347 AM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nThe Gale Watch was upgraded to a Gale Warning and Small Craft\nAdvisories were extended through tonight. Otherwise, no major\nchanges were made to the forecast. \n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Frost and Freeze conditions continue through this morning. \n\n- 2) Uncertainty remains in regards to the track and potential \nimpacts from a nearby Nor'easter this week.\n\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Frost and Freeze conditions continue through\nthis morning. \n\nFreeze Warnings and Frost Advisories remain in effect for much \nof this area east of the Blue Ridge and west of I-95 until 9AM\nthis morning. Temperatures as of 3 AM are in the 30s across much\nof the forecast area west of I-95 with temperatures expected to\nfall a few more degrees before sunrise. As surface high pressure\nsettles over the region, temperatures continue to gradually \nwarm with frost/freeze concerns diminishing.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Uncertainty remains in regards to the track and potential \nimpacts from a nearby Nor'easter this week.\n\nOverall not too much change in the weather pattern this week. With \nan \"Omega Block\" taking form, upper-level atmospheric features \ngenerally remain stuck in place. Current model guidance \ncontinues to depict ridging over the central US and a strong \nhigh building over the Great Lakes through the middle of this \nweek. Although some uncertainty remains in the exact track of \nthe Nor'easter, this pattern tends to keep the developing low \nfar enough off the Mid- Atlantic coast to nearly eliminate \nshower potential across our region through next week. Overall, \nany impactful weather will be tied to coastal communities along \nthe Chesapeake Bay where potential coastal flooding and gusty \nmarine winds remain possible concerns this week. As for these \nmarine and coastal flooding concerns see the corresponding \ndiscussions below. \n\nLate in the week, this Nor'easter is expected to pull away from the \ncoast giving way to another strong high pressure system over our \narea. Heading into next weekend, dry and seasonable conditions are \nexpected to persist.\n\nTemperatures this week remain steady with highs in the mid to \nupper 50s and overnight lows in the upper 30s to mid 40s. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /07Z MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nVFR conditions continue as surface high pressure builds overhead\nand dry conditions persist. Winds remain primarily out of the\nnorth each day with terminals near the airport gusting around 15\nknots in the afternoon. Otherwise, terminals can expect light\nnortherly winds, no precipitation, and VFR conditions. \n\nVFR conditions are expected at all terminals Thursday and \nFriday. Northwesterly winds on thursday generally turn out of \nthe northeast with occasional gusts up to 30 kts, especially \nnear the waters. \n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nThe Nor'easter off the Mid-Atlantic coast will deliver a \nprolonged period of high end SCA conditions and gales (mainly \nover the central/lower waters). The Gale Watch was upgraded to a\nGale Warning for tonight into Tuesday morning. Additionally,\nSmall Craft Advisories were extended through Tuesday morning for\nmost of the waters excluding the upper Potomac. While the threat\nfor gale force winds diminishes after Tuesday, Small Craft\nAdvisories will likely be needed for portions of the waters\nthrough the end of the week.  \n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\nTidal anomalies rise through midweek as a Nor'easter lingers\noffshore. Tidal locations including Dahlgren, Annapolis,\nSolomons Island, and Alexandria are forecast to reach minor\nflood stage by Tuesday or Wednesday high tide cycles. However,  \nconsiderable uncertainty remains on how exactly this Nor'easter \nwill track and subsequently affect the tide levels. Elevated \nwater levels likely won't decline until late in the week due to \nthe stagnant weather pattern. \n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Small Craft Advisory from noon today to 6 PM EDT this evening \n     for MDZ008.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 11 PM this evening to 11 AM EDT \n     Tuesday for MDZ008.\n     Freeze Warning until 9 AM EDT this morning for MDZ004-005.\n     Frost Advisory until 9 AM EDT this morning for MDZ006-503>507.\nVA...Freeze Warning until 9 AM EDT this morning for VAZ051-501-502-\n     505.\n     Frost Advisory until 9 AM EDT this morning for VAZ038>040-050-\n     053-506-526-527.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory from noon today to 6 PM EDT this evening \n     for ANZ530-535-538.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 11 PM this evening to 11 AM EDT \n     Tuesday for ANZ530-538.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 8 AM this morning to 11 AM EDT \n     Tuesday for ANZ531-539.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 11 AM EDT Tuesday for ANZ532-533-\n     537-540>542.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 11 PM EDT this evening for ANZ534-\n     543.\n     Gale Warning from 11 PM this evening to 11 AM EDT Tuesday for \n     ANZ534-543.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 8 AM this morning to 6 PM EDT this \n     evening for ANZ536.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/KVH\nAVIATION...AVS/KVH\nMARINE...AVS/KVH\n"},"forecast":{"t":1792415443,"days":{"2026-10-19":{"hi":66,"lo":48,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-20":{"hi":69,"lo":48,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-21":{"hi":65,"lo":44,"pop":1,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-22":{"hi":67,"lo":48,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-23":{"hi":63,"lo":43,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-24":{"hi":62,"lo":43,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-25":{"hi":65,"lo":46,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1792